 HAM palette entries. Attackers can craft a type-0 CDXL file whose HAM pixels select unfilled new_palette entries in cdxl_decode_ham8() or cdxl_decode_ham6(), exposing stack bytes and pointer fragments in the BGR24 output.","score":6.8,"sev":"medium","published":"2026-11-01T01:17:18.147Z","modified":"2026-11-01T01:17:18.147Z","window_date":"2026-11-01","activity_at":"2026-11-01T03:30:37Z","date_basis":"GitHub advisory publication","affected":[],"refs":[{"label":"NVD record","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-120246","source":"NVD"},{"label":"CVE Program record","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-120246","source":"CVE Program"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24856","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.2/libavcodec/cdxl.c#L226-L229","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/47313ad3f9f33b892384b976fb7c09b3c85fd74e","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-4.4-through-9.0.2-uninitialized-memory-disclosure-via-cdxl-ham-decoder","source":"NVD"},{"label":"GitHub security advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-76cq-jhfp-r489","source":"GitHub"}],"related_cves":[],"advisories":[{"label":"GitHub Security Advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-76cq-jhfp-r489"}],"sources":["NVD","GitHub Advisory Database"],"kev":null,"primary_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-120246","cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","cwe":["CWE-457"]},{"id":"CVE-2026-120245","title":"FFmpeg 0.10 through 9.0.2 contains a use of uninitialized resource vulnerability in sunrast_decode_frame() that leaks heap memory when decoding truncated 1-bit and 4-bit paletted…","desc":"FFmpeg 0.10 through 9.0.2 contains a use of uninitialized resource vulnerability in sunrast_decode_frame() that leaks heap memory when decoding truncated 1-bit and 4-bit paletted Sun Raster images. Attackers can craft a truncated Sun Raster file so the uncleared temporary bitmap is expanded into PAL8 pixels, exposing stale heap contents such as allocator words in decoded output.","score":6.8,"sev":"medium","published":"2026-11-01T01:17:17.960Z","modified":"2026-11-01T01:17:17.960Z","window_date":"2026-11-01","activity_at":"2026-11-01T03:30:37Z","date_basis":"GitHub advisory publication","affected":[],"refs":[{"label":"NVD record","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-120245","source":"NVD"},{"label":"CVE Program record","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-120245","source":"CVE Program"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24877","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.2/libavcodec/sunrast.c#L188-L194","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/356a391bf57df2fb80fd61f2821c8c83d15ce180","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/66b6ca270b33fd74367d7d371f6de16ec664446e","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-0.10-through-9.0.2-uninitialized-memory-disclosure-via-sun-raster-decoder","source":"NVD"},{"label":"GitHub security advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-c346-mwjq-88hv","source":"GitHub"}],"related_cves":[],"advisories":[{"label":"GitHub Security Advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-c346-mwjq-88hv"}],"sources":["NVD","GitHub Advisory Database"],"kev":null,"primary_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-120245","cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI